msg04.mp4	Hi team, Beatrice Artino here, reporting from the too many women's group meeting in Magosio. Today was our monthly table banking day. 25 members attended out of 30. Together they saved 18,000 shillings, and we gave out 4 small loans to members who are starting businesses, mostly selling vegetables and second-hand clothes. The Treasurer, Mama Lucy Kiprop, recorded everything in the book. Our next meeting is on the 15th. If you need the records, Lucy's number is 0745 000 638.
msg05.mp4	Morning everyone, this is Janet Moongi. Yesterday we went to Sarambia Primary School for the menstrual hygiene session with the girls in class 6-8. 60 girls attended. We talked about periods, how to use and dispose of pads safely, and why they should not miss school. At the end, every girl received a pack of reusable sanitary pads. The head teacher, Mrs. Esther Coach, has asked us to come back and also talk to the mothers. Her phone number is 0790-000-274 if someone wants to follow up.
msg06.mp4	Hello team, this is Masi Wambui. I want to share about the community dialogue on gender-based violence we held this afternoon at the Chiefs Camp in Solai. 35 women attended, plus a few village elders. The police gender desk officer, Corporal and Muchua, explained how to report cases and where survivors can get help. Some women shared their stories, but it was very emotional. Three women asked for private follow-up and we connected them with the counselor. For anything about this session, you can call me on 0701 000 593.
msg07.mp4	Hi everyone, sister Nancy share ono here. Today we did the cervical cancer screening camp at Rongai Health Center. We screened 28 women. Most results were normal, but 3 women had positive results, so we referred them to Nakuru level 5 hospital for further treatment. One of them is Mrs. Agnes Wairimu, and she has agreed to go on Monday. on Monday. Please whoever is going to Nakuru that day help her with transport. Her number is 0768000341. I will upload the full report later.
msg08.mp4	E, congratulations to mama pyridijep2 on the new baby. We are so happy for you. Ladies, let's plan to visit her this weekend at her home in Khabarak after church. I suggest we each contribute 200 shillings for a small gift, maybe a baby blanket and some manga. Send your contribution to Ruth on M-Pesa, her number is 0756000819. And please don't forget to bring your own chairs, last time we were standing. Okay, have a blessed evening.
msg09.mp4	Hello team, this is Caroline Naimbura reporting from Campiamoto. Today we held the kitchen garden training for women farmers. 18 women attended. The agriculture officer, Mr. Peter Langat, showed them how to make a sack garden and how to make compost from kitchen waste. Each woman received seedlings of sukuma wiki and spinach to plant at home. Next month we will visit their homes to see how the gardens are doing. If you want to join the follow up visits, call me on 0712 000 765.
msg10.mp4	Good evening, this is Joyce Muthoni. I was helping Sister Nancy at the screening camp in Rongai today. Just adding to her report, we had 28 women screened for cervical cancer, and 3 were referred to Nakuru level 5. The women were very happy because many of them had never been screened before. Next time we should bring more chairs and water because the queue was long. My number is 0729000408 if you need anything from me.
